      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "But you can already do this?\nJust set up your gestures such that it transits to a state with a water gun if you're wearing your beach outfit as dictated by another parameter, and into a state without the water gun if you're not.\nYou can also control layers if you'd prefer to do it that way with the state behaviors Animator Layer Controller and Playable Layer Control. See: https://docs.vrchat.com/docs/state-behaviors\nYou'd have different gestures on different layers, and use the Animator Layer Controller to set which one is the \"active\" one by adjusting its weights. This sounds exactly like what you're asking for, which already exists.",
